The solver will generate initial population of seating arrangements via greedy algorithms and then use evolutionary process to find and improve optimal solutions

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Guest tree + table capacity] --> B[Create initial population]
    B --> C[Evaluate each arrangement]
    C --> D[NSGA-II selection]
    D --> E[Crossover and mutation]
    E --> C
    C --> F[Pareto-optimal seating arrangements]
```


We will train a GNN from the optimal seating arrangements created by the evolutionary algorithm. The GNN will be used to generate part of the initial population above:
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Synthetic or example guest trees] --> B[Run evolutionary optimizer]
    B --> C[Collect strong seating assignments]
    C --> D[Train GNN model]
    D --> E[Save trained weights]
    E --> F[Use GNN to seed part of the initial population]
```

